WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:20.985
Jack had quit the team three days earlier but still hadn't gotten the nerve to tell his parents.

2
00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:26.880
The last three mornings, after his mother drove him to the community center, Jack walked to a coffee shop.

3
00:00:26.881 --> 00:00:30.365
He bought lemonade there and played games on his phone.

4
00:00:30.366 --> 00:00:36.033
After a couple of hours, he wet his hair in the bathroom sink and went outside to meet his mom.

5
00:00:36.034 --> 00:00:39.629
The routine was getting boring and lonely.

6
00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:46.790
Today he sat in the coffee shop and called his best friend in Oklahoma.

7
00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:50.885
"Yo!" Noah said. "Great to hear from you, dude!"

8
00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:52.590
Jack grinned.

9
00:00:52.591 --> 00:00:56.023
"I bet Los Angeles is totally amazing," Noah said.

10
00:00:56.024 --> 00:01:01.513
"How many celebrities have you met? Have you gone surfing? Talked to beautiful girls?"

11
00:01:01.514 --> 00:01:12.102
"Zero, no, and yes," Jack replied. Well, he'd talked to one beautiful girl. But he hadn't seen Laura since he'd quit the swim team.

12
00:01:12.103 --> 00:01:19.006
"Guess who I went out with last night?" Noah said. Before Jack could guess, Noah blurted out the answer.

13
00:01:19.007 --> 00:01:23.417
"Kara. Since you're not around, I asked Kara to the movies."

14
00:01:23.418 --> 00:01:27.906
"Whoa," Jack said. Neither of them had been on a date before.

15
00:01:27.907 --> 00:01:29.766
"It was great!"

16
00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:34.158
"Awesome!" Jack said. "Hey, how did the swim meet go?"

17
00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:39.206
"We won. And I got my personal best time in the backstroke," Noah said.

18
00:01:39.207 --> 00:01:40.903
"Congratulations."

19
00:01:40.904 --> 00:01:47.989
"Oh, and now that our best swimmer—you, of course—is gone, I'm doing breaststroke on the relay team."

20
00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.271
"Cool," Jack said.

21
00:01:50.272 --> 00:01:53.972
"So you talked to some beautiful girls?" Noah asked.

22
00:01:53.973 --> 00:01:57.520
"Just one but we swam together at my pool."

23
00:01:57.521 --> 00:01:59.812
"Awesome," Noah said.

24
00:01:59.813 --> 00:02:04.801
"I should ask her out. If you can get a date, anyone can!" Jack joked.

25
00:02:04.802 --> 00:02:13.285
Noah laughed along. "If you weren't so far away, I'd punch you. So did you totally impress the girl with your swimming?"

26
00:02:13.286 --> 00:02:23.273
"Totally." Jack had lost a race to Laura and done a belly flop in front of her. So he'd definitely made an impression—an awful one!

27
00:02:23.274 --> 00:02:32.599
"I need to go, Noah. Congrats on swimming your personal best. And on dating Kara." Jack clicked off his phone, feeling lonelier than ever.

28
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:40.925
Later Jack's mother drove him home from fake swim practice. Back at the apartment, Luke was playing with one of their new neighbors.

29
00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:47.178
The two little boys ran through the small apartment, waving rubber swords.

30
00:02:47.179 --> 00:02:58.761
Meanwhile the Long-Hair Boys song played over and over through the wall.

31
00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:04.910
Jack clapped his hands over his ears. "Mom, can I go to the pool?"

32
00:03:04.911 --> 00:03:08.092
"Aren't you tired from your practice this morning?"

33
00:03:08.093 --> 00:03:12.417
Jack quickly shook his head. "Nope. I'm feeling great."

34
00:03:12.418 --> 00:03:19.913
"All right," his mother said. "You know the rule: if you're the only one at the pool, you have to come home."

35
00:03:19.914 --> 00:03:30.320
When Jack got to the pool, he groaned. He definitely wasn't the only one there. Mrs. Wilson was sitting on a lounge chair.

36
00:03:30.321 --> 00:03:34.237
He forced himself to be polite and waved to her.

37
00:03:34.238 --> 00:03:42.556
She peered at him, frowning. "Young man, you need to practice if you want to swim faster than your girlfriend."

38
00:03:42.557 --> 00:03:44.088
"She's not my—"

39
00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:53.226
"You should be out here every day. My grandson, little Tommy, once swam 196 days in a row.

40
00:03:53.227 --> 00:03:56.964
He took a few days off only because he got pinkeye."

41
00:03:56.965 --> 00:04:02.295
"Oh," Jack said. He dived into the pool.

42
00:04:02.296 --> 00:04:08.033
"Streamline! Streamline! Streamline!" Mrs. Wilson yelled.

43
00:04:08.034 --> 00:04:16.847
After three laps of the freestyle stroke, Jack stood up at the shallow end of the pool.

44
00:04:16.848 --> 00:04:23.086
"Cup your hands more. Like this." Mrs. Wilson cupped her hands.

45
00:04:23.087 --> 00:04:30.355
"Thank you, Mrs. Wilson." Jack sat on the pool steps and closed his eyes for a few moments.

46
00:04:30.356 --> 00:04:42.167
"‘Listen to my pleas. You're the one for me,'" a girl's voice sang next to him.

47
00:04:42.168 --> 00:04:50.757
Jack's eyes flew open. Laura was standing over him, at the edge of the pool. Had he been humming that awful song again?

48
00:04:50.758 --> 00:04:57.010
She grinned at him. "I love that song! I saw the Long-Hair Boys in concert last year."

49
00:04:57.011 --> 00:05:05.653
"Oh. That song is . . ." Jack tried to think of something good about it. "Um, it's really catchy."

50
00:05:05.654 --> 00:05:11.985
Laura sat on the pool steps, so close to him he could see the cute freckles on her cheeks.

51
00:05:11.986 --> 00:05:15.731
"How come you haven't been to swim practice?" Laura asked.

52
00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:25.301
"I . . . uh . . ." Jack looked away, wondering what the coach had said to the other swimmers. "Well, I had pinkeye."

53
00:05:25.302 --> 00:05:27.122
"Too bad," she said.

54
00:05:27.123 --> 00:05:29.489
"Hi, Jack!" Luke shouted.

55
00:05:29.491 --> 00:05:39.623
Luke and his new friend rushed toward the swimming pool, throwing a beach ball at each other and squealing happily.

56
00:05:39.624 --> 00:05:51.032
"Slow down, boys!" Mrs. Gibson said, hurrying after them with a large mesh bag filled with towels, water bottles, and sunscreen.

57
00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:56.786
"No running near the pool! And keep your voices down!" Mrs. Wilson said.

58
00:05:56.787 --> 00:06:03.920
"Sorry about that," Mrs. Gibson said. She introduced herself to Mrs. Wilson and then looked at Laura.

59
00:06:03.921 --> 00:06:09.093
Laura smiled. "Hi. I'm Laura Perez. I live in apartment 2D."

60
00:06:09.094 --> 00:06:15.185
Jack's mother smiled back. "I'm Anne Marie Gibson. Nice to meet you."

61
00:06:15.186 --> 00:06:22.256
"Jack and I are on the same swim team," Laura said. "My mother was wondering if you'd like to carpool to practices."

62
00:06:22.257 --> 00:06:27.842
Jack's heart sank. He hadn't thought about carpooling!

63
00:06:27.843 --> 00:06:32.743
"It's too bad Jack got pinkeye and missed the last three practices," Laura said.

64
00:06:32.744 --> 00:06:37.994
"Oh no!" Jack thought. He couldn't manage to look at his mom.

65
00:06:37.995 --> 00:06:46.067
"What?" Mrs. Gibson sounded shocked. "Jack didn't have pinkeye. He's been at practice every morning this week."

66
00:06:46.068 --> 00:06:48.443
Laura shot a look at Jack.

67
00:06:48.444 --> 00:06:53.702
Jack's mother looked at him too. "You have been going to practice, right?"

68
00:06:53.703 --> 00:06:55.891
Jack didn't say anything.

69
00:06:55.891 --> 00:07:00.154
"Do I have to call the coach and ask him?" his mother said.

70
00:07:00.155 --> 00:07:10.721
Jack sighed. "I'm sorry, Mom," he mumbled. "I skipped the last three practices. I went to a coffee shop instead."

71
00:07:10.722 --> 00:07:17.300
Jack's mother didn't seem to know what to say. "Obviously, we have some things to discuss later."

72
00:07:17.301 --> 00:07:24.450
"Sorry!" Laura mouthed at Jack. She looked just as confused as Mrs. Gibson.

73
00:07:24.451 --> 00:07:35.619
"My little Tommy would never lie to his mother or skip practice," Mrs. Wilson chimed in. "Young man, you should be ashamed."

74
00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:40.378
Jack was ashamed. But this was his mother's fault too.

75
00:07:40.379 --> 00:07:49.761
She and his father had taken Jack away from his friends and his school and his swimming team in Oklahoma, where Jack had been a star.

76
00:07:49.762 --> 00:07:57.761
Jack had lied, but so had his parents—about his new bedroom and how great life in California would be.

77
00:07:57.762 --> 00:08:08.329
Anger washed over Jack. He felt angry at everyone: his parents for the move. Laura for tattling on him. Mrs. Wilson for being a busybody.

78
00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:18.790
And his little brother, who announced loudly, "I'm peeing in the pool!"
